cff-version: 1.2.0
title: quantum-from-newton
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  manuscript whose figures it reproduces.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dennis M.
    family-names: Heim
    email: physics@d-heim.de
    city: Kaiserslautern
    country: DE
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/demaheim/quantum-from-newton"
abstract: >-
  Simulation of a one-dimensional chain of companion particles moving under
  Newton's equations with a local interaction built from signed inverse
  neighbour gaps. Reproduces the particle-in-a-box and harmonic-oscillator
  stationary densities and the double-slit interference pattern predicted by
  the Schrödinger equation, without adjustable parameters.
keywords:
  - foundations of quantum mechanics
  - Schrödinger equation
  - emergent quantum mechanics
references:
  - type: article
    title: "From Newton's equations to the Schrödinger equation: domain walls as the quantization condition"
    authors:
      - given-names: Dennis M.
        family-names: Heim
